# Kung Pao Chicken

Based on [The Woks of Life](https://thewoksoflife.com/kung-pao-chicken/) and
[Chrissy Teigen Cravings Hungry for More](https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/553580/cravings-hungry-for-more-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman)
([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250616010240/https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/553580/cravings-hungry-for-more-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman/)),
pg. 141

{ rating="5" image="kung_pao_roasted_broccoli.jpeg" }
:::
:::

Includes the Sichuan chicken stir-fry and a roasted broccoli variant.

## Ingredients

### Chicken

#### Peanuts

- [ ] 1 cup [roasted shelled peanuts]{ ing="roasted-shelled-peanuts" }

#### Chicken and Marinade

- [ ] 12 oz [chicken breast]{ ing="chicken-breast" }, cut into 3/4-inch cubes (or boneless skinless chicken thighs)
- [ ] 1 tsp [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-the-marinade" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-marinade" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dry sherry]{ ing="dry-sherry" } (or Shaoxing wine)
- [ ] 1/8 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 pinch [white pepper]{ ing="white-pepper" }

#### Sauce

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [light soy sauce]{ ing="light-soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [dark soy sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [rice wine vinegar]{ ing="rice-wine-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsps [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-sauce" }

#### Stir-Fry

- [ ] 3 Tbsps [oil]{ ing="oil" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, smashed and sliced
- [ ] 2 thin slices [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, minced
- [ ] 2 [chiles de árbol]{ ing="chiles-de-arbol" } or other small dried red chilies, deseeded and chopped (or 1/2 tsp red pepper flakes)
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [ground black pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [ground coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }
- [ ] 6 [scallions]{ ing="scallions" }, white portions only, cut into 3/4-inch pieces

### Roasted Broccoli

#### Broccoli

- [ ] 1/4 cup [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-roasting-broccoli" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil-for-roasting-broccoli" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 2 lbs [broccoli]{ ing="broccoli" } (2 smaller heads)
- [ ] [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper-for-broccoli" }

#### Kung Pao Sauce

- [ ] 1/4 cup [Thai sweet chili sauce]{ ing="thai-sweet-chili-sauce" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [oyster sauce]{ ing="oyster-sauce" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil-for-broccoli-sauce" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-broccoli-sauce" }
- [ ] 1.5 Tbsp [Sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce-for-broccoli-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [unseasoned rice vinegar]{ ing="unseasoned-rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 2 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic-for-broccoli-sauce" }, finely minced

#### Garnish

- [ ] 1/2 cup [chopped salted roasted peanuts]{ ing="chopped-salted-roasted-peanuts" }
- [ ] 1 [thinly sliced scallion]{ ing="thinly-sliced-scallion" }
- [ ] 1 fresh [jalapeno]{ ing="jalapeno" }, sliced into rings

## Recipe

### Chicken Stir-Fry

1. Combine the [chicken]{ ing="chicken-breast" } with 1 tsp each of [oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-the-marinade" }, [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-marinade" }, and [dry sherry]{ ing="dry-sherry" }, 1/8 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and a pinch of [white pepper]{ ing="white-pepper" }. Set aside to marinate for 20 minutes.
1. In a small bowl, mix together [light soy sauce]{ ing="light-soy-sauce" }, [dark soy sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" }, [rice wine vinegar]{ ing="rice-wine-vinegar" }, [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, [water]{ ing="water" }, and [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-sauce" }. Set aside.
1. Heat 2 Tbsps [oil]{ ing="oil" } in a wok or large skillet over high heat. Sear the chicken, remove from the wok to a bowl, and set aside.
1. Turn the heat to low and add another Tbsp oil. Add the [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, [chiles]{ ing="chiles-de-arbol" }, [black pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }, [coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }, and [scallions]{ ing="scallions" }. Cook for 1-2 minutes until fragrant.
1. Add the chicken back to the pan and turn the heat to high. Stir-fry for 1 minute, then stir up the prepared sauce so the settled cornstarch is incorporated. Add the sauce to the wok and stir-fry for another minute; the sauce should thicken very quickly.
1. Add the [peanuts]{ ing="roasted-shelled-peanuts" }, give everything a final stir, and serve.

### Roasted Broccoli Variant

1. Preheat oven or air fryer to 400°F.
1. Cut the [broccoli]{ ing="broccoli" } into florets, stems peeled and cut into 1/4-inch thick rounds.
1. In a bowl, whisk together the [oils]{ ing="sesame-oil-for-roasting-broccoli vegetable-oil-for-roasting-broccoli" } and [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }. Toss the broccoli with the mixture and season with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper-for-broccoli" }.
1. **Oven:** Spread on a rimmed baking sheet and roast until edges are blackened and crisp (20-25 min). **Air Fryer:** Arrange in basket in a single layer (work in batches if needed) and cook until charred and crisp (10-12 min), shaking halfway.
1. Meanwhile, whisk together the [sauce]{ ing="thai-sweet-chili-sauce oyster-sauce sesame-oil-for-broccoli-sauce vegetable-oil-for-broccoli-sauce sriracha soy-sauce-for-broccoli-sauce unseasoned-rice-vinegar garlic-for-broccoli-sauce" } in a medium bowl.
1. **Oven:** Toss broccoli with sauce directly on the pan, then broil until sauce is thick and bubbling (4-5 min). **Air Fryer:** Transfer broccoli to a bowl, toss with sauce, return to air fryer and cook until sauce is thick and bubbling (2-3 min).
1. Transfer to a serving platter and garnish with [peanuts]{ ing="chopped-salted-roasted-peanuts" }, [scallion]{ ing="thinly-sliced-scallion" }, and [jalapeno]{ ing="jalapeno" }. Optionally, serve over rice.

## Notes

- Dry sherry substitutes 1:1 for Shaoxing wine; use chicken broth for alcohol-free.
- Black pepper and coriander approximate Sichuan peppercorn’s aroma without its numbing effect; use 1/2 tsp Sichuan peppercorn powder if available.
- Chiles de árbol are the closest common substitute for Chinese dried chilies; use red pepper flakes if unavailable.
- Boneless skinless chicken thighs can replace the chicken breast.
- The broccoli variant is the rated vegetarian version.
